WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.134
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:27.404 --> 00:31.007
(Francesca Next Door)

3
00:33.076 --> 00:34.678
(All names of people, places, events, and other details are fictitious.)

4
00:34.744 --> 00:36.012
(AI-based technology was used in part of the production.)

5
00:36.279 --> 00:40.984
Sagging skin, pull it tight.

6
00:41.051 --> 00:45.188
Wrinkles, smooth out right.

7
00:51.728 --> 00:53.830
I asked for a facelift,

8
00:53.897 --> 00:56.399
and now they're asking me to give them a cash lift?

9
00:56.466 --> 01:00.971
Honestly, they can sniff out my money like bloodhounds.

10
01:02.806 --> 01:03.807
What's that smell?

11
01:04.674 --> 01:07.611
- Okay, slow. - Take it easy.

12
01:07.677 --> 01:09.012
Be careful.

13
01:09.579 --> 01:11.748
- Watch out. - It's so heavy.

14
01:13.717 --> 01:14.951
Easy now.

15
01:16.953 --> 01:18.054
What's going on?

16
01:19.990 --> 01:21.791
Excuse me, let me through.

17
01:22.759 --> 01:25.261
Excuse me. What is that?

18
01:25.328 --> 01:27.063
I think someone died.

19
01:27.797 --> 01:30.000
Someone died?

20
01:31.468 --> 01:32.469
This way.

21
01:33.370 --> 01:34.404
Easy.

22
01:36.039 --> 01:38.675
Hey, handsome guy with a mustache.

23
01:38.908 --> 01:40.176
What is this thing?

24
01:40.377 --> 01:41.711
It belongs to the new resident here.

25
01:41.778 --> 01:43.179
I'm not sure what it is, ma'am.

26
01:43.246 --> 01:45.615
I'm sorry. "Ma'am?"

27
01:45.682 --> 01:47.417
I'm not that old!

28
01:47.484 --> 01:48.485
Fine, I'm sorry, miss.

29
01:48.551 --> 01:49.586
We'll get moving.

30
01:49.953 --> 01:51.554
Oh, my goodness.

31
01:51.621 --> 01:54.557
What is this in the rain, a coffin-showboating situation?

32
01:55.392 --> 01:56.893
Ladies, isn't it unbelievable?

33
01:56.960 --> 01:58.795
What's happening to our neighborhood?

34
01:58.862 --> 02:00.030
- Oh, right. - Goodness me.

35
02:00.096 --> 02:03.199
I have a very bad feeling about this.

36
02:06.469 --> 02:08.238
Oh, lightning...

37
02:10.273 --> 02:12.175
- Put it down here. - Slowly.

38
02:16.446 --> 02:19.015
Is this person nuts?

39
02:19.516 --> 02:22.018
Who puts a coffin at home?

40
02:22.085 --> 02:24.287
Gosh, it was ridiculously heavy too.

41
02:24.587 --> 02:25.622
That's it, right?

42
02:25.689 --> 02:27.557
- Yeah, let's go. I'm starving. - Okay.

43
02:30.427 --> 02:31.628
What's an ax doing here?

44
02:32.729 --> 02:36.299
What do I know about the psychology of someone who keeps a coffin at home?

45
02:37.467 --> 02:38.468
Let's go.

46
02:42.105 --> 02:43.606
Hey, wait up.

47
02:44.974 --> 02:46.242
Didn't you hear something?

48
02:46.309 --> 02:47.310
What?

49
02:47.777 --> 02:49.179
What did you hear?

50
02:51.815 --> 02:53.550
Maybe I heard it wrong.

51
02:53.883 --> 02:55.118
Let's just go.

52
02:57.087 --> 02:58.888
Okay, wait for me.

53
02:58.955 --> 03:00.023
This feels wrong.

54
03:29.953 --> 03:31.154
What's going on?

55
03:33.923 --> 03:35.358
Oh, you're here.

56
03:35.725 --> 03:36.760
Come sit.

57
03:37.660 --> 03:39.362
There.

58
03:43.166 --> 03:44.801
Let's see.

59
03:44.868 --> 03:46.169
(Name, Jang U Ju Career Interests, Doctor)

60
03:46.236 --> 03:47.971
So your career interests are...

61
03:48.404 --> 03:50.306
neurosurgeon as first choice,

62
03:50.373 --> 03:52.008
OB-GYN as second choice,

63
03:52.242 --> 03:54.277
and orthopedic surgeon as third choice.

64
03:54.344 --> 03:58.615
You're determined to fix whatever's wrong with people.

65
04:01.084 --> 04:02.085
But...

66
04:02.919 --> 04:04.354
do you have to,

67
04:04.888 --> 04:06.189
no matter what,

68
04:06.656 --> 04:07.824
become a doctor?

69
04:10.093 --> 04:12.362
Yes, that's my only goal.

70
04:24.107 --> 04:27.310
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot! - Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

71
04:29.546 --> 04:32.582
But you know...

72
04:32.649 --> 04:35.819
your grades are a bit short of med school standards.

73
04:36.352 --> 04:39.522
"Contradict" means to disagree with...

74
04:39.589 --> 04:42.158
"Contradict..."

75
04:42.759 --> 04:45.094
"Stick to" means to follow...

76
04:45.161 --> 04:46.429
Hey, don't throw it!

77
04:58.374 --> 04:59.442
Sorry, class president.

78
04:59.976 --> 05:01.177
I told you not to.

79
05:04.781 --> 05:08.585
"Be patient" means to keep your cool...

80
05:13.590 --> 05:17.227
"Be patient" means to keep your cool...

81
05:20.063 --> 05:22.298
"Tension" means stress...

82
05:32.442 --> 05:33.710
How about that?

83
05:34.444 --> 05:36.546
Really? I'm down.

84
05:37.280 --> 05:38.982
Hey, see you tomorrow.

85
05:39.415 --> 05:40.416
See you.

86
05:41.050 --> 05:42.051
Bye, class president.

87
05:42.318 --> 05:43.319
Bye, guys.

88
06:08.011 --> 06:10.013
(Hart)

89
06:23.660 --> 06:25.194
(Confused means puzzled Panic means to be overwhelmed...)

90
07:03.333 --> 07:04.334
What the heck?

91
07:04.734 --> 07:06.769
What was that girl's deal?

92
07:10.006 --> 07:11.107
Wait.

93
07:11.174 --> 07:12.275
My vocab notebook!

94
07:18.881 --> 07:20.883
(Hart)

95
07:49.479 --> 07:53.349
Happy birthday to me.

96
07:54.817 --> 07:58.388
Happy birthday to me.

97
08:00.556 --> 08:03.326
Happy birthday, dear...

98
08:06.863 --> 08:09.198
Happy birthday, dear...

99
08:10.166 --> 08:11.534
(Dad)

100
08:16.039 --> 08:17.040
Hi, Dad.

101
08:17.440 --> 08:19.108
Hi, U Ju. It's me.

102
08:19.542 --> 08:21.677
It's morning here. What time is it there?

103
08:22.779 --> 08:23.846
It's late at night.

104
08:23.913 --> 08:25.515
Oh, I see.

105
08:25.581 --> 08:27.016
How's everything?

106
08:27.083 --> 08:29.152
The kids here are really nice.

107
08:29.352 --> 08:31.120
I don't know where they learned Korean,

108
08:31.187 --> 08:34.490
but last time, they even thanked me in Korean.

109
08:34.757 --> 08:36.192
- Aren't they adorable? - Right.

110
08:36.859 --> 08:37.860
I see.

111
08:38.194 --> 08:39.262
Anyway,

112
08:39.328 --> 08:42.732
you can use the card I gave you as much as you like.

113
08:42.799 --> 08:43.833
Got it?

114
08:43.900 --> 08:45.168
So no news from you?

115
08:45.935 --> 08:48.104
- By the way, today is my... - Okay, I'm coming.

116
08:48.504 --> 08:50.873
Sorry, I've got an emergency patient.

117
08:51.240 --> 08:52.809
I'll call you later.

118
08:52.875 --> 08:54.177
Take it easy with your studies.

119
08:54.644 --> 08:56.079
- Bye. - Wait...

120
09:13.930 --> 09:15.765
My parents are both doctors,

121
09:15.832 --> 09:17.667
and they're overseas providing medical aid.

122
09:18.334 --> 09:21.070
Dad is in Uganda, and Mom is in Cambodia.

123
09:24.507 --> 09:26.275
They have all this compassion for humanity,

124
09:26.342 --> 09:28.644
but not much for their own child.

125
09:32.782 --> 09:34.851
My older sister, who's already a doctor,

126
09:34.917 --> 09:37.153
my older brother, who recently became one, have joined them,

127
09:40.590 --> 09:42.425
Thanks to that, I'm always alone at home.

128
09:48.564 --> 09:51.701
I live alone in this big house.

129
09:55.605 --> 09:57.540
"Take it easy with your studies?"

130
10:00.009 --> 10:02.111
I must go to med school to become a doctor.

131
10:02.545 --> 10:03.679
And to get into med school...

132
10:03.980 --> 10:05.281
I have to study.

133
11:03.139 --> 11:05.007
(Alarm)

134
11:07.910 --> 11:11.047
(Dooil High School)

135
11:19.222 --> 11:20.289
What did you do yesterday?

136
11:20.823 --> 11:21.824
You didn't text back.

137
11:21.891 --> 11:23.893
Did you hear about the new student?

138
11:24.260 --> 11:25.261
A foreigner, apparently.

139
11:25.328 --> 11:26.662
- Really? A guy? - Yeah.

140
11:27.263 --> 11:28.331
No, it's a girl.

141
11:30.199 --> 11:31.667
Jeez, look at you.

142
11:31.734 --> 11:34.370
I saw you sleeping. I can't deal with you guys.

143
11:34.437 --> 11:36.405
All right.

144
11:37.273 --> 11:39.775
We have a new student today.

145
11:40.509 --> 11:41.510
I'll bring her in.

146
11:41.777 --> 11:42.778
Come in.

147
11:56.826 --> 11:57.927
That girl is...

148
12:06.035 --> 12:08.437
Why, class president? Do you have something to say?

149
12:09.839 --> 12:10.840
Sorry?

150
12:13.776 --> 12:15.745
No, sir. Never mind.

151
12:15.811 --> 12:17.546
Goodness me.

152
12:18.614 --> 12:20.750
Okay, so...

153
12:20.816 --> 12:22.285
Isn't she the weird girl from last night?

154
12:23.085 --> 12:24.453
So she was a new student?

155
12:25.154 --> 12:27.890
(Pi Na Young)

156
12:28.491 --> 12:31.794
Her name is Pi Na Young.

157
12:32.461 --> 12:34.297
She hasn't been living in Korea.

158
12:34.363 --> 12:36.165
She came from Romania.

159
12:36.666 --> 12:39.535
She may not be used to the Korean culture,

160
12:39.602 --> 12:41.937
so help her out. Understand?

161
12:42.004 --> 12:43.706
- Yes, sir! - Okay, great.

162
12:44.273 --> 12:46.075
Let's see.

163
12:46.309 --> 12:47.643
You see that empty seat?

164
12:47.710 --> 12:48.811
Sit over there.

165
12:50.179 --> 12:51.180
Na Young?

166
12:53.149 --> 12:54.283
Who's Na Young?

167
12:55.584 --> 12:56.585
That's you.

168
12:56.652 --> 12:58.354
Take that seat over there.

169
12:59.322 --> 13:00.389
Right, I forgot.

170
13:01.090 --> 13:02.325
That was my name.

171
13:02.858 --> 13:04.794
Well, thanks, man.

172
13:09.832 --> 13:11.400
- "Thanks, man?" - Well...

173
13:11.467 --> 13:12.868
Okay, now.

174
13:13.769 --> 13:15.938
The mock exam is just around the corner.

175
13:16.005 --> 13:18.207
That means the CSAT is coming up soon.

176
13:19.175 --> 13:20.543
You all need to study.

177
13:21.177 --> 13:22.445
Get ready for class.

178
13:22.978 --> 13:23.979
What did you say?

179
13:24.580 --> 13:25.614
One whole year left?

180
13:25.681 --> 13:28.050
That's not enough time to bring up your grades.

181
13:28.651 --> 13:31.620
Hurry up and open your books, everyone.

182
13:37.259 --> 13:39.595
Whatever she is, I won't get involved.

183
13:43.699 --> 13:46.936
Korean verse is divided into the opening, the middle, and the closing.

184
13:49.238 --> 13:52.508
The closing typically starts with three syllables.

185
13:52.575 --> 13:54.810
Standard Korean verse is...

186
13:54.877 --> 13:56.345
What's the matter?

187
13:57.313 --> 13:59.215
Hey, do you know me?

188
14:00.216 --> 14:02.084
No. Look at the board.

189
14:04.720 --> 14:06.822
I definitely saw you somewhere.

190
14:09.291 --> 14:10.926
I look like a lot of people.

191
14:11.327 --> 14:12.728
I have a pretty generic face.

192
14:13.129 --> 14:14.830
So will you look at the board now?

193
14:15.498 --> 14:17.867
It's part of the closing structure.

194
14:20.870 --> 14:21.937
New student?

195
14:22.471 --> 14:24.673
You should focus on me during class.

196
14:28.978 --> 14:29.979
Fine.

197
14:32.047 --> 14:34.917
Anyway, this is a frequently tested topic. Keep that in mind.

198
14:34.984 --> 14:37.153
You should always aim to get one more question right.

199
14:39.622 --> 14:40.790
Maybe not.

200
15:01.010 --> 15:03.112
- I'll see you next class. - Thank you, sir.

201
15:03.612 --> 15:05.714
Class is over, so...

202
15:35.478 --> 15:36.946
You're from Romania,

203
15:37.012 --> 15:38.614
but you speak pretty good Korean.

204
15:39.248 --> 15:40.916
Didn't you learn to be polite, though?

205
15:41.183 --> 15:43.919
That's only for people above me.

206
15:43.986 --> 15:45.354
Who's above me in this place?

207
15:48.991 --> 15:50.526
You're funny.

208
15:51.760 --> 15:52.795
But hear me out.

209
15:53.262 --> 15:54.930
There's a hierarchy in school.

210
15:55.731 --> 15:57.299
Let me make one thing clear.

211
15:57.900 --> 15:59.368
I'm certainly above you...

212
15:59.435 --> 16:01.070
Gosh, what the heck?

213
16:02.204 --> 16:03.205
By any chance,

214
16:03.906 --> 16:05.307
did you just crawl out of a field?

215
16:05.741 --> 16:08.677
Excuse me, what did you say?

216
16:09.011 --> 16:10.846
You smell like grass.

217
16:13.015 --> 16:14.650
Okay, that's it. I've had it.

218
16:18.020 --> 16:19.655
This is Diptyque.

219
16:19.722 --> 16:21.290
It's super expensive!

220
16:21.991 --> 16:23.092
Really?

221
16:23.158 --> 16:24.159
You like the smell of grass?

222
16:24.226 --> 16:25.394
Interesting taste.

223
16:26.028 --> 16:29.064
Great, I'll start calling you "Grass."

224
16:30.766 --> 16:32.301
Nice to meet you, Grass.

225
16:34.837 --> 16:37.406
- She definitely doesn't know who I am. - She has no clue.

226
16:37.473 --> 16:38.874
Are you crazy?

227
16:41.777 --> 16:43.145
That's a rough way to say hello.

228
16:45.447 --> 16:46.916
Pleasure to meet you, Grass.

229
16:47.917 --> 16:49.318
Why are you just standing there, A Ra?

230
16:49.752 --> 16:51.220
You're out of your mind.

231
16:55.624 --> 16:57.226
Okay, nice to meet you as well.

232
16:59.295 --> 17:01.497
I want to greet you too, but I'm out of hands.

233
17:01.564 --> 17:02.565
Will you wait a minute?

234
17:03.265 --> 17:04.366
Hold on.

235
17:04.433 --> 17:07.303
My scalp is bleeding, Na Young.

236
17:07.369 --> 17:09.138
Okay, I let go. Let's talk it out.

237
17:09.204 --> 17:11.273
Please, I'm sorry.

238
17:11.340 --> 17:13.375
- I already let go. - Please let go.

239
17:13.442 --> 17:16.645
Never get involved.

240
17:18.480 --> 17:19.949
Never get involved.

241
17:20.082 --> 17:21.083
I'm sorry?

242
17:21.150 --> 17:22.718
My point is...

243
17:24.019 --> 17:25.854
You should look out for her.

244
17:26.055 --> 17:27.957
As the class president, got it?

245
17:29.258 --> 17:31.126
- But... - You saw her.

246
17:31.193 --> 17:33.429
She doesn't even know how to speak politely.

247
17:34.029 --> 17:36.398
Help her adjust to life in Korea.

248
17:37.299 --> 17:38.934
Help her find her way around,

249
17:39.234 --> 17:41.503
and do your part as the class president.

250
17:41.904 --> 17:44.440
Okay, I'll do that.

251
17:44.506 --> 17:45.507
Good.

252
17:47.543 --> 17:48.544
Please do.

253
17:52.781 --> 17:54.216
Where's Na Young?

254
17:54.283 --> 17:55.284
What?

255
17:57.119 --> 17:58.120
I don't know.

256
18:00.055 --> 18:01.657
Where did she go?

257
18:06.362 --> 18:07.563
What the heck? You startled me!

258
18:07.997 --> 18:10.466
Hey, why are you in there?

259
18:10.966 --> 18:12.368
This is more comfortable.

260
18:12.434 --> 18:14.136
It feels cozy and familiar.

261
18:14.436 --> 18:15.904
Well, okay. Anyway...

262
18:17.206 --> 18:18.974
If you're stuck with something,

263
18:19.041 --> 18:21.010
just come to me and ask me about it.

264
18:22.745 --> 18:23.746
Ask you?

265
18:25.114 --> 18:26.115
Why?

266
18:27.516 --> 18:29.184
So it's because...

267
18:31.086 --> 18:32.588
I'm the class president.

268
18:33.422 --> 18:34.423
Class president?

269
18:34.490 --> 18:37.092
All right, folks. Sit down.

270
18:38.727 --> 18:40.763
Let's talk later.

271
18:42.464 --> 18:45.200
You'll take a short quiz today.

272
18:45.934 --> 18:48.270
It shouldn't be too hard since we've covered all this.

273
18:48.337 --> 18:51.707
- But it's not fair. - We're not ready yet.

274
18:51.774 --> 18:52.775
What are you doing?

275
18:56.412 --> 18:57.846
Here you go.

276
19:06.655 --> 19:07.856
Hey.

277
19:08.424 --> 19:09.525
Hey.

278
19:10.793 --> 19:12.094
Pass me the...

279
19:24.306 --> 19:26.241
- Hey, teacher. - What?

280
19:26.508 --> 19:28.777
What's the answer to the first question?

281
19:29.244 --> 19:30.312
What?

282
19:31.780 --> 19:33.782
What do you think you're doing?

283
19:34.049 --> 19:36.151
This is a quiz.

284
19:40.089 --> 19:42.758
Isn't it a teacher's job to teach us what we don't know?

285
19:42.825 --> 19:44.827
Well, that's right,

286
19:44.893 --> 19:46.495
but you're taking a quiz.

287
19:47.696 --> 19:48.697
Is that right?

288
19:49.164 --> 19:50.165
Too bad.

289
19:52.334 --> 19:53.335
Hey, class president.

290
19:55.738 --> 19:57.606
What's the answer?

291
19:59.508 --> 20:01.643
You're asking me now?

292
20:02.077 --> 20:04.079
You told me to ask you if I was stuck with something.

293
20:18.327 --> 20:20.496
You can't ask about answers to a quiz.

294
20:27.836 --> 20:29.738
Where is her common sense?

295
20:30.139 --> 20:31.473
She's got absolutely no manners.

296
20:32.975 --> 20:35.477
Let's just get through today.

297
20:36.812 --> 20:39.081
I'll just show her the basics and get it over with.

298
20:43.418 --> 20:44.419
Hey.

299
20:44.720 --> 20:46.388
Don't you have any cash on you?

300
20:46.688 --> 20:48.223
I really don't.

301
20:48.791 --> 20:51.393
Every dime I find on you earns you a smack.

302
20:51.827 --> 20:55.264
Wait, that phrase is ancient, isn't it?

303
20:55.330 --> 20:57.599
Who carries around cash these days?

304
20:57.966 --> 21:01.136
You see, we accept mobile transfers.

305
21:01.503 --> 21:03.272
I'd prefer a fee-free option.

306
21:03.338 --> 21:04.406
What do you think?

307
21:04.740 --> 21:06.542
What are you even...

308
21:07.242 --> 21:08.443
What do you say?

309
21:20.556 --> 21:23.492
It's the law of nature for the strong to prey on the weak.

310
21:24.026 --> 21:25.027
Keep going.

311
21:26.929 --> 21:28.630
Who the heck are you?

312
21:28.697 --> 21:30.599
Isn't that the freaky new student?

313
21:31.333 --> 21:32.868
Oh, the one from Romania...

314
21:33.402 --> 21:35.971
But you look way too Korean.

315
21:36.038 --> 21:37.139
So what?

316
21:37.206 --> 21:39.775
Should I teach you a lesson?

317
21:43.979 --> 21:45.147
What was that?

318
22:07.436 --> 22:08.437
Hey.

319
22:12.941 --> 22:14.810
Who are you now?

320
22:18.480 --> 22:19.481
Hi, Hyeol.

321
22:22.184 --> 22:24.753
Now who do you think you are?

322
22:25.420 --> 22:27.022
You've got something to say to my friend?

323
22:27.089 --> 22:28.357
Not at all.

324
22:29.691 --> 22:31.560
Why are you scared? Who's this guy?

325
22:31.627 --> 22:33.862
Jeez, don't you know Bloody Yoo Hyeol?

326
22:35.998 --> 22:37.933
Oh, shoot. Is that him?

327
22:38.000 --> 22:39.334
Will you answer my question? Who is he?

328
22:39.401 --> 22:41.036
We have to get out of here.

329
22:41.103 --> 22:43.005
Here's all my cash.

330
22:43.071 --> 22:45.741
I can even transfer you some money.

331
22:45.807 --> 22:47.876
- We have to go! - Why?

332
22:47.943 --> 22:49.378
- Let's go. - Wait, but...

333
22:49.444 --> 22:50.913
- Hey... - Bye, guys.

334
22:50.979 --> 22:52.881
Who the heck is he?

335
22:54.283 --> 22:55.284
Bye.

336
22:58.387 --> 23:00.555
I don't have a friend like you.

337
23:01.156 --> 23:02.157
I know.

338
23:02.524 --> 23:04.192
So let's be friends starting today.

339
23:06.762 --> 23:08.563
We'll be pretty good friends.

340
23:09.097 --> 23:10.098
Don't you think?

341
23:15.370 --> 23:16.371
Pi Na Young.

342
23:18.540 --> 23:19.541
Class president?

343
23:21.009 --> 23:23.545
I told you to wait in your seat. When did you come out?

344
23:23.779 --> 23:25.480
Follow me. I'll show you around the school.

345
23:36.992 --> 23:39.661
I'll give you a step-by-step tour of the facilities,

346
23:39.962 --> 23:40.963
so for now...

347
23:44.833 --> 23:46.134
Why do you have that?

348
23:46.368 --> 23:47.536
I like the color red.

349
23:47.903 --> 23:49.338
I like everything red.

350
23:49.738 --> 23:51.340
I like this one. I'll take it.

351
23:51.406 --> 23:52.407
I like how it hugs me.

352
23:52.908 --> 23:54.076
Put it back.

353
23:56.211 --> 23:57.212
What's this?

354
23:57.646 --> 23:58.647
Is this a ring?

355
23:59.014 --> 24:00.015
Wait, hold on.

356
24:06.388 --> 24:07.456
Hey, miss.

357
24:09.658 --> 24:10.659
Hey.

358
24:11.126 --> 24:12.361
You have to pay for those.

359
24:14.696 --> 24:16.431
- Enjoy. - Thank you.

360
24:20.302 --> 24:22.404
You have to line up.

361
24:37.285 --> 24:38.520
(The Private Lives of Vampires)

362
24:41.123 --> 24:43.025
Hush. You have to be silent.

363
24:45.494 --> 24:47.195
I didn't get to study at all.

364
24:47.863 --> 24:49.731
School is so annoying.

365
24:49.798 --> 24:51.366
There are way too many rules.

366
24:53.268 --> 24:55.337
I know you're not from here, but there's a limit.

367
24:55.837 --> 24:57.873
Didn't anyone teach you basic decency?

368
24:58.607 --> 24:59.908
What are you, really?

369
25:00.542 --> 25:01.543
Me?

370
25:02.944 --> 25:04.913
Do you want to know?

371
25:08.517 --> 25:09.518
I'm a...

372
25:20.662 --> 25:21.663
I'm a human being.

373
25:22.330 --> 25:23.665
That's for sure!

374
25:32.007 --> 25:33.408
Okay, this is it.

375
25:34.009 --> 25:35.010
What is?

376
25:36.244 --> 25:37.879
We're outside of school from this point on.

377
25:38.613 --> 25:41.349
I'm only responsible for you on school grounds.

378
25:41.416 --> 25:43.018
Outside, you're on your own.

379
25:44.286 --> 25:46.588
So let's call it a day today.

380
25:46.655 --> 25:47.656
Bye.

381
26:03.371 --> 26:04.372
What's going on?

382
26:05.474 --> 26:06.475
What?

383
26:06.842 --> 26:08.143
Why are you following me?

384
26:08.443 --> 26:09.778
I'm not following you.

385
26:41.209 --> 26:42.244
Are you kidding me?

386
26:43.078 --> 26:44.079
What do you mean?

387
26:44.546 --> 26:45.847
You are following me.

388
26:45.914 --> 26:46.982
I'm not.

389
26:49.851 --> 26:51.820
Fine, which way is your place?

390
26:52.154 --> 26:53.155
My place?

391
26:53.355 --> 26:54.356
That way.

392
26:54.990 --> 26:55.991
(Dalbit-ro)

393
27:09.037 --> 27:10.539
I bet she's gone by now.

394
27:10.872 --> 27:12.974
Jeez, why do I have to deal with her mess?

395
27:13.842 --> 27:15.610
I wasted so much time to chase her off.

396
27:16.611 --> 27:17.946
I'll hurry back home and study.

397
27:20.849 --> 27:21.850
Oh, no.

398
27:44.105 --> 27:45.740
Where's my phone?

399
27:54.883 --> 27:55.917
Na Young?

400
29:00.148 --> 29:02.250
How did you just...

401
29:12.927 --> 29:15.930
(Francesca Next Door)

402
29:15.954 --> 29:17.954
MkvDrama.Net
